# menu-down-up.pad — move a menu selection, once a second, for as long as a short capture lasts.
#
# Written for C5's proof that a scripted press reaches the game: the dialog in save state 3 has two
# entries, so every press flips the selection and the flip is visible in RAM and on screen. The presses
# are 120 ms (3-4 frames at 30 Hz) — long enough that no capture can miss the press entirely, short
# enough that the menu's auto-repeat never starts.
#
# Timing is wall-clock, not frame-exact: which frame a press lands on is not reproducible, and nothing
# that uses this script may depend on it.
press down 120
sleep 1200
press up 120
sleep 1200
press down 120
sleep 1200
press up 120
sleep 1200
press down 120
sleep 1200
press up 120
sleep 1200
press down 120
sleep 1200
press up 120
sleep 1200
press down 120
sleep 1200
press up 120
